      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You raise a critical point about government bias, as intentionally sorting people into \"vulnerable\" categories inherently requires defining who is vulnerable, which can be subjective. However, \"equity\" differs from neutrality because the current reservation of opportunity is skewed; a strict lottery merely accelerates who gets trapped in poverty or forced into dangerous, inaccessible neighborhoods. While a pure random draw treats all applicants the same on paper, it ignores the reality that not all people start from the same place, so true fairness often requires accounting for these existing disparities. A balanced approach should aim for transparency in how those weights are calculated to prevent the project from becoming a tool for political favoritism rather than genuine community aid.",
